   },
   {
    "quote": "Google Search Operators: Full List & Examples",
    "url": "https://www.greengeeks.com/blog/google-search-operators-full-list-and-examples/",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "Google search operators are short commands you add to a query to filter results by site, file type, title text, date, or other attributes. The three most useful for everyday work are site:, filetype:, and quoted exact-match phrases like “annual report 2024”. Together they cover most of the cases where a regular keyword search returns too much extraneous material.",
    "url": "https://www.greengeeks.com/blog/google-search-operators-full-list-and-examples/",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "Most operator names are case-insensitive. SITE: and site: behave identically. Two exceptions matter. OR and AROUND(N) only work in capital letters; lowercase versions are ignored. The parenthetical number in AROUND(N) must be a positive integer with no spaces inside the parentheses.",
    "url": "https://www.greengeeks.com/blog/google-search-operators-full-list-and-examples/",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "Working. OR must be uppercase.",
    "url": "https://www.greengeeks.com/blog/google-search-operators-full-list-and-examples/",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "Working. Strict on punctuation in some cases.",
    "url": "https://www.greengeeks.com/blog/google-search-operators-full-list-and-examples/",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "Working. AROUND must be uppercase.",
    "url": "https://www.greengeeks.com/blog/google-search-operators-full-list-and-examples/",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "OR (capitalised) or the pipe | returns results matching either term. Wrap alternatives in parentheses for clarity: site:example.com (intitle:guide OR intitle:tutorial). The parentheses are not strictly required but they make the query readable when you stack three or more operators.",
    "url": "https://www.greengeeks.com/blog/google-search-operators-full-list-and-examples/",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   },
   {
    "quote": "Case sensitivity for OR and AROUND. Lowercase or is treated as a normal word, so cats or dogs matches pages containing the word “or”. Lowercase around(5) is ignored. Both must be uppercase.",
    "url": "https://www.greengeeks.com/blog/google-search-operators-full-list-and-examples/",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-05"
   }
  ],
